{"format":"local-vault-ai-portable-chunks-v1","version":1,"chunks":[{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Loop.md::0","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Loop.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"feedback loop feedback loop","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Loop.md","fileName":"Feedback Loop.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Feedback Loop","heading":"Document","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"2026-09-05 14:36\n\nStatus: #baby\n\nTags: [[System Dynamics]] [[Live Game Operations]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["System Dynamics","Live Game Operations","Complex System","Reinforcing Loop","Balancing Loop","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Loop.md::1","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Loop.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"feedback loop feedback loop","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Loop.md","fileName":"Feedback Loop.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Feedback Loop","heading":"Feedback Loop","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"A feedback loop exists when changes produced by interacting parts return to influence the conditions that produced them. This circular causality turns a connected process into a [[Complex System]].\n\nThe two broad forms are the [[Reinforcing Loop]], which magnifies a direction of change, and the [[Balancing Loop]], which counteracts deviation. Complex behavior commonly arises from several such loops operating together at different levels and timescales.\n\nA live product creates an operational loop when a team plans a change, develops and deploys it, measures player response, and uses that evidence to decide what follows. The value of speed lies in shortening the complete learning cycle rather than implementation alone.","tags":["baby"],"links":["System Dynamics","Live Game Operations","Complex System","Reinforcing Loop","Balancing Loop","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""},{"id":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Loop.md::2","sourceKey":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Loop.md","sourceType":"markdown","sectionKey":"__none__","sourceSearchName":"feedback loop feedback loop","filePath":"6 - Full Notes/Feedback Loop.md","fileName":"Feedback Loop.md","folder":"6 - Full Notes","title":"Feedback Loop","heading":"References","sectionNumber":"","sectionTitle":"","content":"[[advancedgamedesign.pdf]]\n[[agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf]]","tags":["baby"],"links":["System Dynamics","Live Game Operations","Complex System","Reinforcing Loop","Balancing Loop","advancedgamedesign.pdf","agilegamedevelopment2e.pdf"],"properties":[],"pageStart":0,"pageEnd":0,"embeddingF32":""}]}